engine integration:
  claude:
    unchanged .claude/settings.json
  pi:
    wrote .pi/settings.json: added packages entry npm:@gabo-ai/pi@0.2.6
    gabo refuses to build on Pi without a subagent package:
    Pi has no subagents, so gabo cannot work on Pi without a subagent package. For subagents I recommend gentle-pi, installed with `npm i -g gentle-pi` (adds the `gentle-shell` launcher) or `pi install npm:gentle-pi` (inside plain Pi; npm is used only because gentle-pi's postinstall needs it); another subagent package is acceptable. As the recommended setup I recommend the full Gentle AI framework (https://github.com/Gentleman-Programming/gentle-ai): its methodology with RDD and the Engram memory stack, set up for Pi with `gentle-ai install --agent pi`. Then ask me to rebuild.
  opencode:
    removed opencode.json default_agent: "gabo-assistant" (runtimes.assistant is claude, pi)
you still need to:
  - claude: trust this project folder in Claude Code so the gabo-ai marketplace and the gabo plugin apply
  - claude: ask your agent to build the agents (the main session needs .claude/agents/gabo-assistant.md)
  - pi: trust the project in Pi so it installs and loads @gabo-ai/pi from .pi/settings.json
  - pi: install a subagent package (see the refusal above)
